  "label": "The text 'when cops see an unarmed black youth:' is mapped onto the visual depiction of the two police officers.",
  "description": "The textual phrase 'when cops see an unarmed black youth:' directly refers to the visual entities (the police officers) as the agents performing the action described. The officers are visually depicted as the 'cops' who are 'seeing' (implied by their pointing and attention) an unseen target, which is mapped to the 'unarmed black youth' mentioned in the text. This creates an analogical mapping where the officers are the 'cops' in the scenario described by the text.",
